== Service pattern ==

Line F operates two service patterns between [[Sant Cristòfor]] and [[L'Estany (CristoCarril)|L'Estany]]:

{| class="wikitable"
|-
! Service !! Stops !! Stations served !! Travel time
|-
| '''Express''' || 1, 2, 10, 13 || Sant Cristòfor Central Terminal to L'Estany, skipping intermediate stations || ~75 min
|-
| '''Local''' || All stops 1–13 || Sant Cristòfor Central Terminal to L'Estany || ~100 min
|}

The '''express''' service provides the fastest connection between Sant Cristòfor and L'Estany, stopping at the Central Terminal, Portal de Sant Cristòfor, Polígon Sud, and L'Estany. The express bypasses all intermediate stations in the switchback section between Polígon Sud and L'Estany, reducing the end-to-end journey to approximately 75 minutes. The express is primarily used by long-distance commuters and visitors travelling between Sant Cristòfor and the lakeside resort communities of the L'Estany comarca.

The '''local''' service stops at all 13 stations along the full 85.4 km route, with an end-to-end journey time of approximately 100 minutes. The local provides the only CristoCarril service to the intermediate stations in Sant Jordi — Estadi, Carretera del Camp, Plaça dels Pins, and Polígon Sud — as well as the switchback section stations La Colònia and Coll Alt, which serve the rural eastern districts of Sant Cristòfor comarca and the highland pass area.

== Schedule ==

Line F operates from approximately 5:00 AM to 12:30 AM daily. Frequencies vary by service pattern and time of day:

{| class="wikitable"
|-
! Service !! Peak (7–10 AM, 4–7 PM) !! Off-peak (daytime) !! Evening (after 8 PM) !! Weekend
|-
| '''Express''' || every 30 min || every 60 min || every 90 min || every 60 min (daytime), every 90 min (evening)
|-
| '''Local''' || every 60 min || every 90 min || every 120 min || every 90 min (daytime), every 120 min (evening)
|}

The express provides a regular connection between Sant Cristòfor and L'Estany, with reduced evening and weekend frequency. The local is the least frequent, reflecting the lower ridership at the intermediate stations in the switchback section and the long end-to-end journey time. The two-car train restriction on the switchback section limits capacity on all services. Combined, the two services provide up to 3 trains per hour at the Central Terminal during peak periods.

== Fares ==

Line F uses the [[Tarifa Integrada]] fare system, which is shared across the CristoCarril network and integrated with the [[Metro de Sant Cristòfor]] and [[Rodalies de Portnou]] systems. The line operates a flat fare of B$2.50 for all journeys, regardless of distance travelled.

Passengers using a [[Tarifa Integrada]] smart card receive free transfers to connecting metro, streetcar, and Rodalies services within a 90-minute window. Concession fares (half price) are available to seniors, students, and children under 12. Children under 5 travel free. Monthly and weekly passes are available with discounts of up to 40% off the single-ride fare.

